      "stdout": "Replace one slot inside an added template segment.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --ref TEXT          Unified draft reference\r\n          --template-seg-id TEXT \r\n                              Raw template segment id\r\n          --slot TEXT REQUIRED \r\n                              Replaceable slot id returned by `draft template slots`.\r\n          --resource TEXT     Replacement media resource, e.g. local:///abs/video.mp4 or\r\n                              /abs/video.mp4.\r\n          --content TEXT      Replacement text content for text slots.\r\n          --inherit TEXT      Inherit source segment properties for media slots (true/false,\r\n                              default true).\r\n          --sync-group        Also apply the replacement to grouped slots in the same template\r\n                              group.\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  # Replace a media slot with a local video file\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft template replace --ref local://demo --template-seg-id <seg> \\\r\n      --slot <slot_id> --resource local:///abs/video.mp4\r\n  # Replace a text slot with new content\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft template replace --ref local://demo --template-seg-id <seg> \\\r\n      --slot <slot_id> --content \"New title\"\r\n  # Replace a media slot without inheriting props, syncing grouped slots\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft template replace --ref local://demo --template-seg-id <seg> \\\r\n      --slot <slot_id> --resource local:///abs/video.mp4 --inherit false --sync-group\r\n",
